-- title:
--   Two ends of the blow-up chart on one component coincide
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q\ge 5$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which (`hK`) is the $L$-subextension generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and group $H=$[`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, that is, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q$ in its maximal ideal (`hAq`) and with $\xi$ in the image of $A\to L$ (`hξA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hϖ`) and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=qu$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C=$`chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$ (the finite $j$-chart), and $X=$[`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the pushout of the two chart spectra over $\operatorname{Spec}A$. Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a Drinfeld-chart witness at all relevant points; its conclusion is a conjunction of seven clauses, summarised here) asserts: for every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure map to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ mapping to $z$ whose ideal is supersingular in the above sense, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with maximal ideal generated by $\sigma(\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$, such that: constants from $A$ go to $C(\sigma a)$; every automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ realising the level action of $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) with data $(q\ell,\xi,q\ell,(q\ell)^2M',H)$, preserves $C$; such $\tau$ with $\gamma$ also in $\Gamma(\ell)$ induce the identity modulo $y'$; for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ inducing the identity modulo $y'$ there are an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a scalar $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ compatible with $\tau$ through $e$ and the canonical map from $C$ to the completed stalk, $\theta$ fixing constants, $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of $(X_0,X_1)$, $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$, $M\equiv c\gamma$ entrywise modulo the maximal ideal of $W$, $c\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ containing $C(\sigma\varpi)$, not containing both $X_0$ and $X_1$, with tangent forms $a_1X_0+b_1X_1$ and $a_2X_0+b_2X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ satisfying $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to the stalk; for a prime of $S$ with tangent form $X_0$ the corresponding contraction contains the germ of $a\in C$ exactly when every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$; and the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $j$-expansion with all exponents multiplied by $q\ell$) lies in $C$, is congruent modulo $y'$ to some $a_0\in A$, and the image of the difference in $S$ is the class of a series $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0\ge1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form takes unit values at all pairs $(a,b)\in W^2$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q$ in the maximal ideal of $W$.
--
--   Next a point $z$ of $X$ is fixed together with the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ above $z$ (`hy'`) which is supersingular (`hss'`) and satisfies $y'=y$ (`hy'y`), together with a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ with $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\bigr)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` states for this data exactly the seven clauses listed above.
--
--   The remaining data are: an ideal $J$ of $C$ which (`hJ`) is the infimum of all ideals obtained, for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ realising the level action of $\gamma^{-1}$ and preserving $C$, by pulling the ideal generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$ in $S$ back along $e_1$ composed with the completion map and the canonical map $C\to\mathcal O_{X,z}$, and then along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$; the $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ which (`hB`) is generated over $C$ by the elements $x$ with $x\varpi_t\in J$; and a valuation subring $W$ of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). Further hypotheses: `hR1` states $C\le B$ and that every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ of elements of $B$ with $h\ne0$; `hR2` states that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ precisely when $b$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$, and that $W$ is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h$ a unit of $W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) states that for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements of $B$ in the maximal ideal of $W$, compatible with the residue map of $A$ and equivariant for level automorphisms through the [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) of pairs $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), with $c\ne1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; that level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ receives the centre of $W$ under some level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ all of whose level translates lie in the centre of $W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Call a subring $O$ of $K$ an *end* if there exist $a\in J$ with nonzero image in $K$ and, setting $B_a$ to be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over $C$ by the elements $x$ with $xa\in J$, a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$, such that $O$ consists exactly of the elements $f$ of $K$ of the form $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$ and $h\notin P$; every element of $y$ that lies in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$; and $B$ is not contained in $O$. Call a prime ideal $\mathfrak q$ of $O$ a *trace of $\mathfrak p$* (for an ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $C$) if $\varpi$ lies in $\mathfrak q$ whenever it lies in $O$, some element $b$ of $y$ has its image outside $\mathfrak q$ whenever that image lies in $O$, and for every $c\in C$ whose image lies in $O$ one has $c\in\mathfrak p$ if and only if that image lies in $\mathfrak q$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts: for all subrings $O,O'$ of $K$, if $O$ is an end and $O'$ is an end, then for every ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $C$ which is prime, contains the image of $\varpi$, is contained in $y$ and is different from $y$, if $O$ admits a prime which is a trace of $\mathfrak p$ and $O'$ admits a prime which is a trace of $\mathfrak p$, then $O=O'$.
--
--   In the geometry of the integral model of the modular curve at the supersingular point $y$ in residue characteristic $q$, this says that the strict transform of a branch through $y$ meets the exceptional Drinfeld curve in at most one point: two ends of the blown-up chart whose distinguished primes have the same trace $\mathfrak p$ on the $j$-chart are the same local ring. It is one conjunct of the exceptional-fibre description [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.blowupChart_primes_over_supersingular_exceptional_generic_or_end_on_unique_component_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.blowupChart_primes_over_supersingular_exceptional_generic_or_end_on_unique_component_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked).
